      en: "Taliouine is perched at an altitude of nearly 1,200 meters in the heart of the Anti-Atlas mountains and is celebrated globally as the 'Saffron Capital' of Morocco. The town sits in the shadow of Jbel Sirwa, an extinct volcanic massif whose nutrient-rich volcanic soil provides the ideal environment for the cultivation of Crocus sativus. Every October and November, the saffron harvest brings the entire community together for the labor-intensive process of picking and drying the precious crimson threads by hand. Saffron from Taliouine is consistently ranked among the highest quality in the world, holding a protected designation of origin due to its potency and aroma. Historically, Taliouine served as a vital station on the trade routes connecting the Souss Valley with the Sahara, a past reflected in the ruins of the grand Glaoui Kasbah. Today, the local economy is bolstered by saffron cooperatives, almond production, and a growing ecotourism sector that attracts trekkers bound for the Sirwa peaks.",
